        <b>How this is kept honest, in four rules.</b>
        One review per school, enforced by the database and not by a form. It
        publishes itself a day after it is written, so there is no approval queue
        for inconvenient reviews to sit in. We can only take one down for
        something like spam or naming a child, never for being critical, and
        every removal is recorded with its reason and its rating in our own audit
        log. And the average below counts every published review, with the full
        spread of ratings printed beside it, so a curated average would be
        obvious from the shape of it.
